Flavio Cardone wrote:
> Hello -
>
> how do you make a pudding farm? You hit one to make it multiply? But what if
> you kill it instead of getting it to divide?
>
Get one of the following: a knife, a key or an orcish helm. Other weak
iron objects will work, but it must be iron or you can not split a
pudding. Engrave with it until it refuses to do so (for sharp objects
only, this lowers their enchantment), then dip it into water until it
stops rusting. #name it Puddingbane, make sure it isn't cursed and
wield it as your weapon. Make sure gauntlets of power are off if you
own a set. If you have a stethoscope handy use it to monitor the HP of
your puddings.

Now, go and split one. Puddings have in the range of 50-75 HP in my
experience; splitting them divides the HP evenly between them both. If
they have below 3 HP they will have difficulty splitting and will be
killed off with repeated pokes. Don't split a pudding farm into
extinction, allow them time to recover HP and rotate between puddings.

If they're still dieing after all these precautions, you're simply not
giving them enough time to regenerate.



